 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000

wildos-settings (0.1.54) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Privacy and security > Advanced protection: extra protection for
    people who want it, in one page. Ignore new USB devices while
    locked, the fingerprint needing your password after a restart and
    every so many hours, restart when left locked, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth
    switching themselves off, encrypted DNS with a choice of Quad9,
    Mullvad or Cloudflare, block
    everything unless the VPN is on, the clipboard forgetting passwords,
    presenting mode and password-locked USB sticks, with Reset to
    defaults.
  * Strict protection also asks for the password after 24 hours of
    fingerprint sign-in and restarts a PC left locked for 18 hours.
    Maximum asks for it after 12 hours, and also switches Wi-Fi and
    Bluetooth off when unused and encrypts DNS on every network.
    Anything you set on Advanced protection stays as you set it.
  * Block new USB devices and the VPN kill switch are the same switches
    as their rows on Advanced protection.
  * Encrypted DNS can be switched off on Advanced protection, which puts
    each network back on its own DNS, unencrypted. Switching it back on
    gives every network the encryption it had before.
  * Restart when left locked can close open apps anyway after the time is
    up, for when an app with unsaved work would otherwise keep the PC from
    restarting. Unsaved work in those apps is lost. Waiting for apps to
    close stays the default.
  * History lists each time an app used the camera or microphone, with when
    it started and stopped. This week on the taskbar's camera and
    microphone light opens History showing just those.
  * Accounts leaves out the Guest account while Guest session is on, so
    it can't be made an administrator or deleted by hand.

